        "content": "## Peak Endurance Model\n\n| Metric | What it measures | Why it matters |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Critical Speed (CS)** | Fastest sustainable velocity \u2014 the aerobic steady-state ceiling | The single best predictor of endurance race performance |\n| **D\u2032 (D-prime)** | Finite work capacity above CS | How many surge metres you have available above threshold |\n| **Efficiency Factor (EF)** | Speed per heartbeat (m/s \u00f7 avgHR) | Rising EF = getting faster for the same cardiac cost |\n| **CS:VO2max ratio** | Fraction of aerobic ceiling you can sustain | Higher ratio = better endurance adaptation |\n| **Cardiac Cost (hrTSS/km)** | Stress per kilometre | Lower = more efficient |",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
